\ cv8b.4 - byte-granular dictionary headers for CV8.
\
\ Loaded AFTER cv8.4. Everything in the header that was a cell, or was
\ padded to a cell, becomes bytes:
\
\     [link: 1-3 bytes, tag LAST][count][name chars][body]
\
\ The link is a distance backward from this word's nfa to the previous
\ word in the same thread, encoded like a CV8 call but read from the
\ END - the tag byte sits at nfa-1 because it is the first byte anyone
\ reads:
\
\     tag < 0x80        1 byte    d = tag                        0..127
\     0x80 <= tag < 0xC0  2 bytes   d = (tag & 0x3F) << 8 | [nfa-2]  14 bits
\     tag >= 0xC0       3 bytes   d = (tag & 0x3F) << 16
\                                   | [nfa-2] << 8 | [nfa-3]        22 bits
\
\ and d = 0 is the end of the chain. Reading backward is unambiguous for
\ the same reason reading a forward-tagged field forward is: the tag is
\ always the first byte read. Every consumer of a link in this system
\ starts from a known nfa - the chain walk, >NAME, nothing else - so
\ there is no case where the field has to be found by scanning.
\
\ WHY. Measured, the 64-bit CV8 image was 2.8 KB larger than the 32-bit
\ one for the SAME token stream: 1,088 bytes of link cells, 496 of name
\ padding, 660 of end-of-body padding. None of that is code. With the
\ link a couple of bytes and nothing padded, the call scale can drop to
\ 0 as well, and the image gets the size the byte stream always implied.
\
\ WHAT MOVES. The kernel's SEARCH-WORDLIST compares names a CELL at a
\ time and relies on the nfa being cell-aligned and zero-padded; both go
\ away here, so it is replaced by a byte compare. NAME> loses its
\ ALIGNED. HEADER has to write the link AFTER parsing the name, since
\ the length of the link depends on which thread the name hashes to.
\ >NAME is untouched: it scans back from the body for the count byte and
\ reaches it before the link either way.

0 CV8-SHIFT-V !          \ byte-aligned call targets: base + v
-1 CV8-DOES-FAR? !       \ ...so DOES> needs the three-byte call form
3 CV8-DOES-RESERVE !     \ ...and CREATE must leave room for it

\ ---- the link -------------------------------------------------------
: LINK-LEN ( d --- n )
  DUP 128 U< IF DROP 1 EXIT THEN
  16384 U< IF 2 ELSE 3 THEN ;

: LINK, ( d n --- )
\ Append a link of exactly n bytes, tag byte last.
  DUP 1 = IF DROP C, EXIT THEN
  DUP 2 = IF DROP DUP 255 AND C, 8 RSHIFT 128 OR C, EXIT THEN
  DROP DUP 255 AND C, DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C, 16 RSHIFT 192 OR C, ;

: NEXT-NFA8 ( nfa --- nfa' )
\ The previous word in this thread, or 0 at the end of the chain.
  DUP 1- C@                                    ( nfa tag )
  DUP 128 U< IF DUP IF - ELSE 2DROP 0 THEN EXIT THEN
  DUP 192 U< IF 63 AND 8 LSHIFT OVER 2 - C@ OR - EXIT THEN
  63 AND 16 LSHIFT OVER 2 - C@ 8 LSHIFT OR OVER 3 - C@ OR - ;

\ ---- the header -----------------------------------------------------
: NAME>8 ( nfa --- xt )
\ The body follows the name directly. No ALIGNED.
  COUNT 31 AND + ;

: >BODY8 ( xt --- a-addr )
\ The kernel's >BODY is `CELL+`, which is only right when the body is
\ cell-aligned. The parameter field is at align(body+3) on every path
\ - see CREATE8 and the engine's DOVAR - so compute exactly that.
  CV8-DOES-RESERVE @ 1+ + ALIGNED ;

VARIABLE HDR-HEAD
VARIABLE HDR-LEN

: HEADER8 ( --- )
\ Parse the name first - WORD leaves it counted at HERE - then work out
\ the link, move the name up to make room, and write the link into the
\ gap. The name is at most 31 bytes, so the move is trivial.
  32 WORD DUP FIND IF ." Redefining: " HERE COUNT TYPE CR THEN DROP DROP
  HERE COUNT CURRENT @ @ HASH 1+ CELLS CURRENT @ + @ HDR-HEAD !
  \ The link's length depends on the distance, and the distance depends
  \ on where the nfa lands, which depends on the link's length. Bound it
  \ from above: the nfa is at most HERE+3, so size the link for that and
  \ the real distance always fits.
  HDR-HEAD @ IF HERE 3 + HDR-HEAD @ - LINK-LEN ELSE 1 THEN HDR-LEN !
  HERE DUP HDR-LEN @ + HERE C@ 1+ CMOVE>
  HDR-HEAD @ IF HERE HDR-LEN @ + HDR-HEAD @ - ELSE 0 THEN HDR-LEN @ LINK,
  HERE LAST !
  HERE C@ 1+ HERE C@ 128 + HERE C! ALLOT ;

\ ---- the search -----------------------------------------------------
: NAME=? ( a1 a2 u --- flag )
\ BEGIN/WHILE rather than ?DO: the kernel never uses ?DO itself, so the
\ translator has no case for it, and a word it cannot translate is
\ copied as data and would run as garbage.
  BEGIN DUP WHILE
    >R OVER C@ OVER C@ = 0= IF R> DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
    1+ SWAP 1+ SWAP R> 1-
  REPEAT DROP 2DROP -1 ;

: SEARCH-WORDLIST8 ( c-addr u wid --- 0 | xt 1 | xt -1 )
\ Same contract as the kernel's, byte compare instead of cell compare,
\ and NEXT-NFA8 instead of a cell link. The thread is picked exactly as
\ before: the hash and the wordlist layout are unchanged.
  ROT ROT NAME>BUF
  DUP >R NAMEBUF COUNT R@ @ HASH 1+ CELLS + @ R> DROP   ( nfa )
  BEGIN DUP WHILE
    DUP C@ 31 AND NAMEBUF C@ = IF
      DUP 1+ NAMEBUF 1+ NAMEBUF C@ NAME=? IF
        DUP NAME>8 SWAP C@ 64 AND IF 1 ELSE -1 THEN EXIT
      THEN
    THEN
    NEXT-NFA8
  REPEAT ;
